                    "date": "28/11/2026",
                    "time": "15:00-17:00",
                    "venue_id": "st-nicholas-priory-exeter",
                    "name": "Dynamic Landscapes in Storytelling",
                    "description": "Through fun and challenging on-your-feet exercises, games, and discussions, this workshop acts as a tonic for the storytellers' creative toolkit! Everyone is encouraged to play and improvise as they re- examine their stories and re-vitalise them through a creative connection with dynamic landscapes.\n\n\n\nWorking solo, in partners and in groups, the exercises aim to identify the archetypal spaces in a story, peel back the layers to expose emotional connections, and create word pools to conjure up the invisible world of the story.\n\n\n\nAnd we will examine the question, 'Where in this landscape is the storyteller?'\n\n\n\nIt will be exciting! Bring your notebooks, bring your story and bring your enthusiasm!",
